## Implementation (2026-10-24)

1. **Re-centre on rotation.** The article screen now has a one-shot
   `LaunchedEffect(listState)` that, when speech is actively playing, calls the
   same `scrollToCurrentTop()` the "jump to current" control uses. Because a
   rotation recreates the activity (resetting the LazyColumn scroll) while the
   ViewModel keeps `activePosition`, this restores the follow-along view. It's a
   no-op when nothing is playing / a new article is opened (speech is stopped
   first).

2. **Portrait lock (default on).** New setting "Display → Lock to portrait"
   (default true). A per-activity override via `Activity.requestedOrientation`
   is a supported way to lock one app to portrait even while the device's
   auto-rotate is on — verified against the Android `ActivityInfo` API. Applied
   through the new `OrientationLock` helper in every activity's `onCreate` (and
   `onResume` in `MainActivity`) so the toggle takes effect immediately when
   returning from Settings.

